WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.525
In under two minutes, you will add a sponsor and its logo to your contest.

00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:05.625
We start on the map.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:09.859
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:14.072
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:14.072 --> 00:00:16.562
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.562 --> 00:00:17.907
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.661 --> 00:00:21.877
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.877 --> 00:00:22.529
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.064 --> 00:00:28.560
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.777
See the three dots?

00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:30.325
Tap them.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.893
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.585 --> 00:00:36.214
Tap Mine.

00:00:36.214 --> 00:00:38.163
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:41.864
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.864 --> 00:00:43.232
This is your dashboard.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.548
Tap Sponsors.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.865
Type the sponsor's name, and choose a tier.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.467
Add their website, and choose their logo.

00:00:59.805 --> 00:01:00.890
Tap Add sponsor.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.100
Sponsors can pay you directly, and payment never affects who wins.

00:01:07.026 --> 00:01:09.778
To check how it looks, tap See it as voters do.

00:01:11.758 --> 00:01:15.136
Next up: Presenting installer and quote requests.
